+`VICTORY_RECOVER_REMOVAL=1` opts into forensic capture (default off).
+After removal, a separate instance of this executable suspends every title
+process thread except a dedicated termination watchdog, then clones readable
+cloneable RAM and copies committed saves/storage under `<title data>/recovery`.
+The parent save mutex is held before suspension; a busy save is skipped and
+makes the generation incomplete. No capture, hashing or disk writes occur
+on a surviving title/frame thread. Guard flags are removed only in the clone.
+
+Every generation starts with a flushed `PARTIAL` marker. A loader must reject
+that marker even if `COMPLETE` exists, and reject every `.partial` directory.
+Each artifact is hashed while written; the `COMPLETE` manifest is written last,
+then the directory is renamed and `PARTIAL` removed. There is no exit-time
+artifact readback: verify hashes offline before using forensic evidence. A failed
+or externally killed capture keeps its partial generation and all older ones.
+
+The shared monotonic deadline starts at helper launch: 2,000 ms by default.
+`VICTORY_RECOVERY_BUDGET_MS` can select 50–10,000 ms. A dedicated watchdog in
+each process enforces it even if clone, read, flush or logging stalls, or the
+helper dies. Before cloning, an estimate includes readable committed RAM and
+save/storage file sizes: 250 ms + bytes / 64 MiB/s. This is a conservative
+admission policy, not measured throughput; oversize work exits early. Deadline
+exit is `0xE0680002`. Configure below the external watchdog; an external kill
+before our deadline can still interrupt any stage and cannot be prevented.
+
+These are **FORENSIC ONLY**, never loadable save states. The RAM file header
+(`SCARLRAM2FORENSIC_ONLY\n`) and each generation's README say so. Suspension
+is sequential and freezes arbitrary interrupted updates: title object graphs,
+allocator metadata, descriptors, command/fence bookkeeping and save buffers
+can already be inconsistent. After suspension, title writers stop, but kernel
+I/O, external writers and shared mappings can still change. Non-cloneable or
+inaccessible mappings, OS handles and GPU-only state are absent. RAM, committed
+saves and storage are not an atomic checkpoint; unsaved progress is not guaranteed.
+
+This build makes zero automatic title restart/replay attempts. Device children
+remain cached and lost GPU writes have no replayable safe point. Successful
+forensic capture exits `0xE0670001`; incomplete capture exits `0xE0670002`.
+One JSON event records artifacts, outcome and actual folder when reporting
+finishes within budget; a hard deadline can leave only `PARTIAL`. Keep all
+generations and never copy partial files over live saves. With the flag off,
+legacy handling remains. WARP reconstruction is an isolated no-title probe,
+not evidence of live title resume.
 
